From: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 05:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: starfive: visionfive2-v1.2a: disable EEE on gmac1

The second Ethernet port of the VisionFive 2 v1.2A (gmac1, RMII) has a
Motorcomm YT8512 100 Mbit/s PHY, which runs with the Generic PHY driver.
With a link partner that supports EEE, 100BASE-TX EEE is negotiated and
the link drops every few seconds as soon as the port transmits:
TCP upload falls to 0.1-5 Mbit/s and 50-90% of UDP packets are lost.
With EEE disabled (ethtool --set-eee eth1 eee off) it does 94 Mbit/s in
both directions with no link drop.

Signed-off-by: Paul Spooren <mail@aparcar.org>
---
 arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-starfive-visionfive-2-v1.2a.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-starfive-visionfive-2-v1.2a.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/starfive/jh7110-starfive-visionfive-2-v1.2a.dts
@@ -24,3 +24,7 @@
 	rx-internal-delay-ps = <1900>;
 	tx-internal-delay-ps = <1350>;
 };
+
+&phy1 {
+	eee-broken-100tx;
+};
